      "description_evidence": "The package cookiecutter before 2.1.1 are vulnerable to Command Injection via hg argument injection. When calling the cookiecutter function from Python code with the checkout parameter, it is passed to the hg checkout command in a way that additional flags can be set. The additional flags can be used to perform a command injection.",
      "cause": "An attacker-controlled checkout value is interpreted as a Mercurial option.",
      "preconditions": [
        "Application calls Cookiecutter with untrusted checkout and the hg backend."
      ],
      "prevention": "Separate the hg option list from the checkout value with its supported end-of-options marker.",
      "patch_alignment": "aligned",
      "alignment_note": "Argument-list subprocess invocation without a shell does not prevent target-program option injection. Backend-specific boundary required.",
