      ],
      "description_evidence": "This affects the package celery before 5.2.2. It by default trusts the messages and metadata stored in backends (result stores). When reading task metadata from the backend, the data is deserialized. Given that an attacker can gain access to, or somehow manipulate the metadata within a celery backend, they could trigger a stored command injection vulnerability and potentially gain further access to the system.",
      "cause": "Result metadata selects a callable that is invoked as an exception constructor.",
      "preconditions": [
        "Attacker can manipulate result-backend metadata and a consumer reconstructs the stored failure."
      ],
      "prevention": "Require the reconstructed object to be a class derived from BaseException before invoking it.",
      "patch_alignment": "aligned",
      "alignment_note": "This is callable reconstruction from stored metadata, not a generic shell=True signature. Backend access is a required precondition.",
