      ],
      "description_evidence": "An insecure deserialization vulnerability exists in the BentoML framework, allowing remote code execution (RCE) by sending a specially crafted POST request. By exploiting this vulnerability, attackers can execute arbitrary commands on the server hosting the BentoML application. The vulnerability is triggered when a serialized object, crafted to execute OS commands upon deserialization, is sent to any valid BentoML endpoint. This issue poses a significant security risk, enabling attackers to compromise the server and potentially gain unauthorized access or control.",
      "cause": "A public endpoint can accept a pickle media type and deserialize unsafe input.",
      "preconditions": [
        "Untrusted request reaches the affected entry service; internal and external service boundaries differ."
      ],
      "prevention": "Reject the pickle media type at the main service boundary before deserialization.",
      "patch_alignment": "aligned",
      "alignment_note": "Patch has an is_main guard, not a global pickle ban. No regression test file was found in this patch; runtime coverage remains pending.",
